PHASE 4: ORG SCOPING + TRANSFERS + AUDIT (4-6 days)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Scope lock (updated after production issues)
- This phase is split into two clear layers for content ownership:
  1) **Organization pool assignment** (Super Admin): assign content to an organization only.
  2) **User assignment inside organization** (Org Admin/Manager): assign/shift org-pooled content to members.
- Super Admin does **not** directly assign org content to end users in this phase’s primary flow.

Features
- Org-scoped listing/query updates for:
  - angles, angle templates, pages, integrations and relevant profile sections.
- **Org pool first** assignment flow:
  - Super Admin assigns selected content to `organization_id` only (no direct user assignment in this step).
  - Org admin then assigns to org members.
- Visibility model for org content:
  - Org Admin/Manager can view all content in their organization (pool + user-assigned).
  - Members can view only content assigned to themselves.
- Legacy compatibility:
  - Handle rows with null `organization_id` (pre-org era) without blocking assignment.
  - Do not require pre-existing source assignment to move into org pool.
- Super Admin cross-org clone path (member move remains in Phase 3C).
- Audit logging write path for transfer/clone operations:
  - actor_user_id, action, entity_type, entity_id, from_org_id, to_org_id, metadata, created_at.
- UI clarity:
  - Show `Organization` column in relevant lists (e.g., Angles), display `-` when unassigned.

Acceptance (must all pass)
- Super Admin assigns content to org pool; content appears under that org context.
- Org Admin login for target org can see all org-assigned items (including items assigned to any org user).
- Member login sees only member-assigned items; org pool items are hidden until assigned.
- For legacy null-org rows, assignment to org succeeds and becomes visible in target org.
- No cross-org visibility leakage.
- Every transfer/clone operation creates an immutable audit record.

